stAssurance-prefixed Go tests in the selected local package; derive its declaration from actual source, including valid external test packages. The controller runs Go directly. Emit CA_EVENT JSON using fmt.Println or t.Log. Dependencies are offline; inspect actual source before using internal APIs.\"\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/adapters/runners/experiment.py:117:    \"\"\"Extract complete CA_EVENT lines, preserving runner-provided stream ownership.\"\"\"\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/adapters/runners/experiment.py:122:    marker = \"CA_EVENT \"\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/adapters/runners/cargo.py:19:    harness_instructions = \"Write Rust #[test] integration tests using the captured crate's public API and existing dependencies. The controller fixes the workspace lock and tools; build reuse is specific to a manifest, integration test target and saved build basis. Switching crates may require a first heavy dependency build. Consult research.json build_inputs for preparation evidence and current seed availability; unlisted targets are not known to be prepared, and available seeds still require execution-time validation. Only the generated test target runs, serially with --nocapture and --locked --offline. Emit complete CA_EVENT JSON lines. Helpers are workspace-relative; never replace manifests, locks, build scripts or Cargo configuration. No extra feature flags are added; original dev-dependencies can enable additional features. Actual compiler-artifact records describe reuse; declaration syntax does not establish active cfg branches or private-state reachability.\"\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/adapters/runners/python.py:9:    harness_instructions = \"Use Python imports from the current isolated workspace and print CA_EVENT JSON containing actual returned values.\"\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/SKILL.md:12:Harness prerequisites name observed conditions. Monitor.admission_alias identifies admitted operations whose completion is owed; explicit alias references establish causal predecessors, not array order. Correlate input/result using independent identity, never the compared value or a changing context. Do not repeat results as prerequisites or filter applicability on the result. Missing identity/completion, parse loss, unreached setup and unsupported temporal expressions stay gaps. A complete local witness may coexist with missing independent operations, never same-witness ambiguity. For S implies E, independently observe S and E; S=false is bounded non-occurrence, not proof of E, and missing is not false.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
